{"id":"mahabharata-7-077","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":77,"title":"सप्तसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 77 · Krishna points out Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Krishna draws Arjuna's attention to Duryodhana, who has come out alone in his armour and is in a perilous state. He urges him to strike the proud prince, who has done wrong from the beginning, while Duryodhana's troops advance noisily.","kn":"ಒಬ್ಬನೇ ಕವಚಧಾರಿಯಾಗಿ ಬಂದಿರುವ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನನ್ನು ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ತೋರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಆರಂಭದಿಂದಲೂ ಅನ್ಯಾಯ ಮಾಡಿದ ಆ ಗರ್ವಿಗೆ ಹೊಡೆಯಲು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಸೈನ್ಯ ಗದ್ದಲದೊಂದಿಗೆ ಮುಂದುವರಿಯುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"कृष्ण अर्जुन को कवचधारी अकेले आए दुर्योधन की ओर इंगित करते हैं और आरम्भ से अन्याय करने वाले उस अभिमानी पर प्रहार करने को कहते हैं। दुर्योधन की सेना शोर के साथ आगे बढ़ती है।","te":"ఒంటరిగా కవచధారియై వచ్చిన దుర్యోధనుని కృష్ణుడు అర్జునునికి చూపి మొదటి నుండి అన్యాయం చేసిన ఆ గర్వితుని కొట్టమని చెబుతాడు. దుర్యోధనుని సేన గోల చేస్తూ ముందుకు వస్తుంది.","ta":"கவசம் அணிந்து தனியே வந்த துரியோதனனைக் கண்ணன் அர்ஜுனனுக்குக் காட்டி, தொடக்கத்திலிருந்தே அநீதி செய்த அவ்வகங்காரனைத் தாக்கும்படி வலியுறுத்துகிறார். துரியோதனனின் படை ஆரவாரத்துடன் முன்னேறுகிறது.","ml":"കവചമണിഞ്ഞ് ഒറ്റയ്ക്ക് വന്ന ദുര്യോധനൻ അപകടാവസ്ഥയിലാണെന്ന് കൃഷ്ണൻ അർജുനന്റെ ശ്രദ്ധയിൽപ്പെടുത്തുന്നു. ആദ്യം മുതൽ തെറ്റ് ചെയ്ത ആ അഹങ്കാരിയായ രാജകുമാരനെ അടിക്കാൻ അദ്ദേഹം അർജുനനോട് പറയുന്നു; ദുര്യോധനന്റെ സൈനികർ ബഹളത്തോടെ മുന്നേറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.77; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"वासुदेव उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vasudeva said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"सुयोधनमतिक्रान्तमेनं पश्य धनंजय ।\nआपद्गतमिमं मन्ये नास्त्यस्य सदृशो रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look, Dhananjaya, Suyodhana has come past us. I think he has fallen into danger; there is no chariot-warrior equal to him."}},{"n":2,"text":"दूरपाती महेष्वासः कृतास्त्रो युद्धदुर्मदः ।\nदृढास्त्रश्चित्रयोधी च धार्तराष्ट्रो महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He shoots from afar, a great archer, trained in weapons, battle-mad, firm in weapons, a varied fighter, Dhritarashtra's mighty son."}},{"n":3,"text":"अत्यन्तसुखसंवृद्धो मानितश्च महारथैः ।\nकृती च सततं पार्थ नित्यं द्वेष्टि च पाण्डवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brought up in great comfort and honoured by great chariot-warriors, he is accomplished, Partha, and always hates the Pandavas."}},{"n":4,"text":"तेन युद्धमहं मन्ये प्राप्तकालं तवानघ ।\nअत्र वो द्यूतमायातं विजयायेतराय वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think the time has come for you to fight him, sinless one. Here the gamble between you has come, for victory or for the other."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्र क्रोधविषं पार्थ विमुञ्च चिरसंभृतम् ।\nएष मूलमनर्थानां पाण्डवानां महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here, Partha, throw off the poison of anger stored for so long. This great chariot-warrior is the root of the Pandavas' misfortunes."}},{"n":6,"text":"सोऽयं प्राप्तस्तवाक्षेपं पश्य साफल्यमात्मनः ।\nकथं हि राजा राज्यार्थी त्वया गच्छेत संयुगम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here he is, come within your reach; see your own success. How else would a king who wants a kingdom come to battle with you?"}},{"n":7,"text":"दिष्ट्या त्विदानीं संप्राप्त एष ते बाणगोचरम् ।\nस यथा जीवितं जह्यात्तथा कुरु धनंजय ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune he has come within the range of your arrows; so act, Dhananjaya, that he gives up his life."}},{"n":8,"text":"ऐश्वर्यमदसंमूढो नैष दुःखमुपेयिवान् ।\nन च ते संयुगे वीर्यं जानाति पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bewildered by the pride of power, he has never known sorrow, and he does not know your prowess in battle, bull among men."}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वां हि लोकास्त्रयः पार्थ ससुरासुरमानुषाः ।\nनोत्सहन्ते रणे जेतुं किमुतैकः सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, the three worlds with gods, asuras and men do not dare to conquer you in battle; how much less Suyodhana alone?"}},{"n":10,"text":"स दिष्ट्या समनुप्राप्तस्तव पार्थ रथान्तिकम् ।\nजह्येनं वै महाबाहो यथा वृत्रं पुरंदरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune he has come near your chariot, Partha; kill him, mighty-armed, as Purandara killed Vritra."}},{"n":11,"text":"एष ह्यनर्थे सततं पराक्रान्तस्तवानघ ।\nनिकृत्या धर्मराजं च द्यूते वञ्चितवानयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He has always been bold in doing harm to you, sinless one; he cheated Yudhishthira at dice by trickery."}},{"n":12,"text":"बहूनि सुनृशंसानि कृतान्येतेन मानद ।\nयुष्मासु पापमतिना अपापेष्वेव नित्यदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many most cruel deeds, giver of honour, have been done by this evil-minded man to you, who were always blameless."}},{"n":13,"text":"तमनार्यं सदा क्षुद्रं पुरुषं कामचारिणम् ।\nआर्यां युद्धे मतिं कृत्वा जहि पार्थाविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Make up your mind to a noble course in battle, Partha, and without hesitation kill that ignoble, ever-petty man, who does as he likes."}},{"n":14,"text":"निकृत्या राज्यहरणं वनवासं च पाण्डव ।\nपरिक्लेशं च कृष्णाया हृदि कृत्वा पराक्रम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering in your heart the seizing of the kingdom by trickery, the exile in the forest, and Krishna's humiliation, show your valour, Pandava."}},{"n":15,"text":"दिष्ट्यैष तव बाणानां गोचरे परिवर्तते ।\nप्रतिघाताय कार्यस्य दिष्ट्या च यततेऽग्रतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune he is moving within the range of your arrows; by good fortune he strives in front to resist your task."}},{"n":16,"text":"दिष्ट्या जानाति संग्रामे योद्धव्यं हि त्वया सह ।\nदिष्ट्या च सफलाः पार्थ सर्वे कामा हि कामिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune he knows he must fight with you in battle; and by good fortune, Partha, all your cherished wishes are fulfilled."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्माज्जहि रणे पार्थ धार्तराष्ट्रं कुलाधमम् ।\nयथेन्द्रेण हतः पूर्वं जम्भो देवासुरे मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore kill the Dhritarashtra son, lowest of his family, in the battle, Partha, as Indra once killed Jambha in the war of gods and asuras."}},{"n":18,"text":"अस्मिन्हते त्वया सैन्यमनाथं भिद्यतामिदम् ।\nवैरस्यास्यास्त्ववभृथो मूलं छिन्धि दुरात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With him slain by you, let this leaderless army be broken. Let this be the concluding bath of this enmity; cut the root of the evil-minded."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"तं तथेत्यब्रवीत्पार्थः कृत्यरूपमिदं मम ।\nसर्वमन्यदनादृत्य गच्छ यत्र सुयोधनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha said to him: So be it; this is my own task. Disregarding everything else, go where Suyodhana is,"}},{"n":20,"text":"येनैतद्दीर्घकालं नो भुक्तं राज्यमकण्टकम् ।\nअप्यस्य युधि विक्रम्य छिन्द्यां मूर्धानमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"by whom the kingdom, free of thorns, was enjoyed by us for so long. May I, fighting in battle, cut off his head."}},{"n":21,"text":"अपि तस्या अनर्हायाः परिक्लेशस्य माधव ।\nकृष्णायाः शक्नुयां गन्तुं पदं केशप्रधर्षणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"May I, Madhava, be able to set my foot, in return for the undeserved torment of Krishna, on the head that dragged her by the hair."}},{"n":22,"text":"इत्येवं वादिनौ हृष्टौ कृष्णौ श्वेतान्हयोत्तमान् ।\nप्रेषयामासतुः संख्ये प्रेप्सन्तौ तं नराधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Speaking so, those two Krishnas, glad, sent the best white horses on in the battle, seeking that king."}},{"n":23,"text":"तयोः समीपं संप्राप्य पुत्रस्ते भरतर्षभ ।\nन चकार भयं प्राप्ते भये महति मारिष ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching them, your son, O best of the Bharatas, did not show fear, though a great fear had come."}},{"n":24,"text":"तदस्य क्षत्रियास्तत्र सर्व एवाभ्यपूजयन् ।\nयदर्जुनहृषीकेशौ प्रत्युद्यातोऽविचारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kshatriyas there honoured him for this, that he went out to meet Arjuna and Hrishikesha without hesitation."}},{"n":25,"text":"ततः सर्वस्य सैन्यस्य तावकस्य विशां पते ।\nमहान्नादो ह्यभूत्तत्र दृष्ट्वा राजानमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then from your whole army, O lord of men, a great shout arose there, seeing the king in the battle."}},{"n":26,"text":"तस्मिञ्जनसमुन्नादे प्रवृत्ते भैरवे सति ।\nकदर्थीकृत्य ते पुत्रः प्रत्यमित्रमवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that terrible uproar of the people, your son, slighting his foe, held him back."}},{"n":27,"text":"आवारितस्तु कौन्तेयस्तव पुत्रेण धन्विना ।\nसंरम्भमगमद्भूयः स च तस्मिन्परंतपः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Held back by your son the bowman, Kunti's son grew still more furious, the scorcher of foes, against him."}},{"n":28,"text":"तौ दृष्ट्वा प्रतिसंरब्धौ दुर्योधनधनंजयौ ।\nअभ्यवैक्षन्त राजानो भीमरूपाः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the two, Duryodhana and Dhananjaya, in mutual fury, the kings, grim in aspect, looked on from all sides."}},{"n":29,"text":"दृष्ट्वा तु पार्थं संरब्धं वासुदेवं च मारिष ।\nप्रहसन्निव पुत्रस्ते योद्धुकामः समाह्वयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Partha and Vasudeva enraged, my lord, your son, as if laughing, wishing to fight, called them out."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततः प्रहृष्टो दाशार्हः पाण्डवश्च धनंजयः ।\nव्याक्रोशेतां महानादं दध्मतुश्चाम्बुजोत्तमौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Dasharha and the Pandava Dhananjaya, glad, shouted a great shout and blew their best conches."}},{"n":31,"text":"तौ हृष्टरूपौ संप्रेक्ष्य कौरवेयाश्च सर्वशः ।\nनिराशाः समपद्यन्त पुत्रस्य तव जीविते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing those two joyful, the Kauravas everywhere lost hope for your son's life."}},{"n":32,"text":"शोकमीयुः परं चैव कुरवः सर्व एव ते ।\nअमन्यन्त च पुत्रं ते वैश्वानरमुखे हुतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All those Kurus fell into great grief and thought your son as good as offered into the mouth of fire."}},{"n":33,"text":"तथा तु दृष्ट्वा योधास्ते प्रहृष्टौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nहतो राजा हतो राजेत्यूचुरेवं भयार्दिताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Krishna and the Pandava so glad, the warriors, tormented by fear, said: The king is slain, the king is slain!"}},{"n":34,"text":"जनस्य संनिनादं तु श्रुत्वा दुर्योधनोऽब्रवीत् ।\nव्येतु वो भीरहं कृष्णौ प्रेषयिष्यामि मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing the people's cry, Duryodhana said: Put away your fear; I will send the two Krishnas to death."}},{"n":35,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा सैनिकान्सर्वाञ्जयापेक्षी नराधिपः ।\nपार्थमाभाष्य संरम्भादिदं वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to all the soldiers, the king, hoping for victory, in fury spoke these words to Partha."}},{"n":36,"text":"पार्थ यच्छिक्षितं तेऽस्त्रं दिव्यं मानुषमेव च ।\nतद्दर्शय मयि क्षिप्रं यदि जातोऽसि पाण्डुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said: Partha, whatever divine and human weapon you have learned, show it quickly on me, if you are indeed born of Pandu."}},{"n":37,"text":"यद्बलं तव वीर्यं च केशवस्य तथैव च ।\nतत्कुरुष्व मयि क्षिप्रं पश्यामस्तव पौरुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whatever strength and valour you have, and Keshava as well, use it quickly on me; let us see your manliness."}},{"n":38,"text":"अस्मत्परोक्षं कर्माणि प्रवदन्ति कृतानि ते ।\nस्वामिसत्कारयुक्तानि यानि तानीह दर्शय ॥","meaning":{"en":"They tell of deeds you did out of our sight, done in the service of your master. Show here those deeds."}}]}]}